WEBVTT

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:05.210
<i>Haruko-san returned to Switzerland 
like nothing had happened,</i>

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:08.230
<i>and Ren's first summer 
vacation in Japan began.</i>

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:11.120
I'm on the bridge in the park.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.590
It's okay. I didn't bring Tanuki with me.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:14.740
Do you know the place?

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.880
<i>Yeah, I can see you from over here.</i>

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:18.450
<i>I'll be right— Whoa!</i>

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:19.240
Kiri?

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:21.950
Ren, behind you!

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:22.790
Huh?

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:00.050
What? A job?

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.010
You want one?

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:04.570
I'm just going to help tidy up 
the old man's apartment.

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:05.750
That's okay, right?

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:10.020
Sure, but is there something you want?

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:12.120
Is your allowance too small? 
If that's the case, I can—

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:12.770
No.

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:15.520
Oh, right, you'll be needing a computer soon!

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:17.720
Haruko left me one.

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:19.800
What? Really? Why, then?

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:21.880
Bro, that's enough.

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:24.000
Ren's not a little kid.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.390
It's totally normal for 
him to have a job or two.

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:27.930
And it's your former landlord.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.600
He helped you out, didn't he?

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:33.420
Ren could never deny a request 
from someone you owe so much to.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.350
What is this? You guys, too?

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:36.920
You're just overprotective.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:40.050
But you brought this up out of nowhere.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:42.030
Are you sure there isn't 
something you want?

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:44.050
Tell me the truth, okay?

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:47.180
Even if there was, I wouldn't tell you.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:48.300
Wha—

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:51.190
This unpleasant way of 
speaking, this attitude...

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.540
Is he in his rebellious phase?

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.190
A rebellious phase?

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:01.950
I'm not sure that unpleasant 
little shit was ever agreeable.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.250
Don't call my youngest brother a little shit!

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:08.490
That's not something a girly man who's been 
drinking since this morning should be saying.

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:10.460
Shut up, you tsundere brother-lover!

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:11.860
What did you call me?!

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:13.580
I understand how he feels, though.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:16.670
The first thing I bought with the money 
I made from working was an adult game.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:18.590
I could never tell my family.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:20.270
What?

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:23.340
I-I'm not saying that's what Ren Ren wants...

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.640
Anyway, Ren Ren's a young man now.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.930
He must want more things 
than money could ever buy.

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:33.600
Yet all <i>your </i>money disappears to unexplained 
ends, and you've got no savings.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:34.730
You're so mean.

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:38.490
Maybe his reason's actually a girl.

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:40.440
I saw that girl who was just here.

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:42.600
She was boyish and cute.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.240
Now that I think about it,

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:48.240
she reminded me a bit of Haruko-san.

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:51.840
Thanks for helping me the other day.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:54.750
It's fine. I'm used to big dogs.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:59.000
Since that day, he's been docile around you.

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:01.130
You just have to train them.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:02.830
Really?

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:06.260
Since he showed up, our living room 
has been on the verge of ruin.

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:10.200
Every day, I'm woken up by my mom's 
screams and my dad running around.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:12.520
Why did you suddenly decide to get a dog?

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:16.150
My parents said it had always been 
their dream to have a big dog,

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:19.310
so they just brought him home one day.

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:22.900
You're lucky. Tanuki's so quiet, 
it's like he's not even a dog.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:25.000
I think the same thing sometimes.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.910
He sleeps all day. He's like a cat.

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:30.500
Cats are wilder than that.

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:32.340
Ren, Kiri-chan.

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:35.930
You shouldn't stand out here forever. 
Why don't you come in?

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:37.030
It's hot out here.

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:38.490
Kiri has her dog.

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:40.130
You can bring him in.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:42.550
The heat outside must be 
even worse for the dog.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.640
If you don't behave, I'll throw you out.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:47.880
Kiri-chan, you'll have lunch here, right?

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:49.870
Really? Lucky me.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:51.240
Is this your family's dog?

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:54.060
Yeah, Ren's training him right now.

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:57.350
He's unruly, he bites, and he 
doesn't listen to anything I say.

00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:59.060
He's beyond my control.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.570
He's unruly, he bites, and he doesn't listen, eh?

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:06.990
I bet that inspires you to train him right.

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:10.450
After all, you understand 
how dogs feel, right?

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:11.950
His Past Self

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:14.860
Haru, you're in the way. 
Get back to work.

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:17.670
Okay. Come to the café if you get hungry.

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:22.160
I haven't seen your brother in a while,

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:25.470
but he really is a little 
different from other guys.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:27.280
I'm not sure what you mean.

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:30.250
The ladies who live in the 
area like your brother, too.

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:33.690
He's handsome, has a good personality, 
and on top of that, grew up overseas.

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:36.430
He could've made money as a model.

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:37.530
Really?

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:39.850
By the way, how did that go?

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:41.750
I got his permission.

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:44.760
You don't have to get a job. 
It's my responsibility.

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:47.490
It's fine. It's a good opportunity 
to try working, anyway.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.210
And Haru won't say no if it's 
for our former landlord.

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:52.740
Why don't you at least tell him why?

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:54.650
I don't need to.

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:56.430
<i>What reason could they be talking about?</i>

00:05:56.980 --> 00:05:58.250
Brother dear?

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:01.770
Could you at least not look 
like a parent who's anxious

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:06.010
because his son brought home 
his girlfriend for the first time?

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:06.010
...What is this embarrassing scene?

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:10.700
Huh? But Kiri-chan's cute and 
kind of resembles Haruko-san.

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:12.230
She's dangerous.

00:06:12.230 --> 00:06:14.010
You're more dangerous than any of us.

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:17.140
What makes you say that?

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:20.330
Wait, are you actually serious?

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:24.780
My first floor tenant ran off 
while I was in the hospital.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.480
And the room is a mess.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:30.310
I thought you could help me clean it up.

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:31.150
Got it.

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:35.790
But I never noticed someone living on the 
first floor when I lived on the second.

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:39.810
Come to think of it, that Sasaki guy 
who moved in after you guys left...

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:40.790
Ikuyoshi?

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:43.260
He came to see me sometimes,

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:47.010
but I could never tell if he was home or not.

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:50.160
In the end, he didn't 
pay rent for six months.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:50.800
Huh...

00:06:56.660 --> 00:07:00.970
See? I told you it was a mess.

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:04.790
His clothes stink.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:06.070
Ren! Ren!

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:07.500
What?

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:12.570
What the heck did you do 
in the old man's apartment?

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:15.520
Cleaned, although we didn't 
make it past the entryway.

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:16.690
Are you going tomorrow, too?

00:07:16.690 --> 00:07:19.580
Yeah. I promised to keep 
going until we finished.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.290
The old man should hire a professional.

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:25.060
He said they're expensive.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:30.150
Your first job doesn't have 
to be something so filthy.

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:31.130
If you need money—

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:32.840
You already gave me permission.

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:36.350
I promised I'd help him until we finished.

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:38.810
You're too overprotective, Haru.

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:42.350
<i>He was so right, I couldn't say anything.</i>

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:48.110
<i>But when he's being this stubborn, 
it always means he's hiding something.</i>

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:49.860
What?

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:53.960
Nothing. Hey, Ren, why don't we 
go somewhere this Sunday?

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:56.940
You haven't been outside Tokyo 
since coming to Japan, right?

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:58.120
I've been to Narita.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:07:59.120
That's the airport.

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:03.080
You're just taking him? 
Isn't that discrimination?

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:05.210
Besides, he doesn't like crowds, right?

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:07.400
Let's go someplace really far away.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:08.880
You've got a car.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:11.600
I was just talking about a day trip.

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:14.040
It'll be fine. Shima and 
I have licenses, too.

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:17.940
What idiot issued you a license?

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:19.640
If you want a fight, I'll give you one.

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:20.890
I don't mind going out.

00:08:21.170 --> 00:08:23.080
But I can't this Sunday.

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:26.650
We just started cleaning the 
apartment, and I'm seeing Kiri.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:30.620
Kiri-chan's your classmate, right?

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:32.150
You used to go to school together.

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:36.950
Yeah, she asked me to show her 
family how to handle Lyuba.

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:40.160
If Ren can't go, then we'll 
have to go another day.

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:42.310
I guess you're right.

00:08:42.740 --> 00:08:45.710
<i>It should be a good thing that Ren's starting</i>

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:48.170
<i>to pay attention to the outside world, but...</i>

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:52.170
Did Ren already go to sleep?

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:54.700
Yeah, he said he was 
heading out early tomorrow.

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:55.820
Huh.

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:59.100
The loser who's sulking because 
the baby brother won't give him

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:00.530
any attention is still awake over there.

00:09:00.530 --> 00:09:01.180
Gross.

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:05.440
Shut up. You don't understand how I feel.

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:09.450
I'll never understand the feelings of a man 
who's just short of being a criminal.

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:12.510
They're too complicated for us to understand.

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:14.720
Don't you think that's a little mean?

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:17.900
Why would you say that? 
I just adore Ren, that's all.

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:21.700
Bro, what kind of relationship 
do you want with him, anyway?

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:24.460
That came out of nowhere.

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:26.320
No, it didn't.

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:30.020
Ren's feelings haven't changed 
since he first came to Japan.

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:34.470
Didn't you know that when you 
brought him back from Canada?

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:35.470
What does that mean?

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:39.400
Ren's just playing along with your 
dream to live with your family.

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:42.220
He decided to live in Japan just for you.

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:44.680
It's not like you guys opposed it.

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:46.250
Of course not.

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:49.690
It's Ren's decision, and as 
long as Ren's okay with it,

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:53.520
we don't care what kind of 
relationship he has with you.

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:56.600
But we can see it's not working out that way.

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:57.480
Why not?

00:09:57.480 --> 00:09:58.470
Because you're an idiot.

00:09:58.470 --> 00:09:58.990
Huh?

00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:05.000
Bro, you'd do anything to keep
Ren by your side, right?

00:10:05.260 --> 00:10:07.760
Huh? Of course.

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:12.890
That's the problem.

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:14.710
What? How is that a problem?

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:17.150
I should take a bath and go to bed.

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:18.210
I'm going to sleep, too.

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:19.860
Hey, what's wrong with you two?

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:20.760
What's the problem?

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:25.950
Figure it out, moron!

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:33.770
They're so mean.

00:10:45.070 --> 00:10:45.840
Haru?

00:10:46.150 --> 00:10:48.070
Sorry. Did I wake you?

00:10:48.590 --> 00:10:49.390
No.

00:10:49.390 --> 00:10:51.380
Are you going to the old 
man's apartment tomorrow?

00:10:51.770 --> 00:10:52.690
Yeah.

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:57.040
He wants to bring in an interior decorator 
next month, so we have to hurry.

00:10:57.040 --> 00:10:58.310
I see.

00:10:58.870 --> 00:10:59.490
Ren.

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:03.890
Can I touch you? Just a little.

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:05.930
Ha—

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:07.290
Sorry. I know you're tired.

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:09.930
But it's just a little bit.

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:11.020
I don't mind if you sleep.

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:12.180
Haru?

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:16.500
Lately, we haven't had much time together

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:20.110
since Haruko-san came and 
I've been busy with work.

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:22.580
Sorry about earlier.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:23.800
For what?

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:25.240
This Sunday.

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:30.290
It's fine. Your summer 
vacation has just started.

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:36.210
<i>Is it my fault he's started making this face?</i>

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:39.180
<i>But that's what I really want.</i>

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:43.360
<i>I don't actually just want to be nice.</i>

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:47.310
<i>No, I want to be nice, 
but I also want to be cold to him.</i>

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:50.280
<i>I don't want to make him cry, but I do.</i>

00:11:50.280 --> 00:11:52.710
<i>I don't want to hurt him, but I do.</i>

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:56.770
<i>After all, there's no one else like him.</i>

00:11:57.840 --> 00:11:58.470
Haru?

00:11:58.470 --> 00:12:00.540
Sorry for waking you.

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:01.780
That's all for today.

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:05.780
Can't turn 
back now,
in more ways 
than one

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:02.590
Huh?

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:05.780
You have to be up early tomorrow, right?

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:08.300
I'll wake you up when I get up.

00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:09.150
Huh?!

00:12:09.150 --> 00:12:10.790
I'm satisfied. Goodnight.

00:12:10.990 --> 00:12:11.830
<i>Wha...</i>

00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:16.360
<i>Th-This guy is the worst!</i>

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:22.680
Now this is a problem.

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:25.300
This place's selling point is that face.

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:28.060
I have a good idea how that happened, though.

00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:30.080
Haru-chan, what happened to your face?

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:32.960
Oh, my youngest brother's going 
through a rebellious phase.

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:33.810
Cute, right?

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:36.220
I don't understand why he's smiling.

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:38.450
Something smells fishy.

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:42.820
Ren's right straight this 
morning was a sight to behold.

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:46.820
He made the clean hit and then 
left him with a parting shot.

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:50.620
Don't you lay a finger on me!

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:53.560
Haru-san, you can't do that.

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:57.060
Seriously? He's in no position 
to be criticizing me.

00:13:00.070 --> 00:13:01.590
Hey, Ren!

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:02.960
Gramps?

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:05.150
I came to get you for lunch.

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:06.880
Do you like eel?

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:10.670
Since it's the Day of the Ox, 
I'll get you some eel.

00:13:10.670 --> 00:13:12.410
But it's not Saturday.

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:14.940
And you eat eel on the Day of the Ox?

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:17.980
Ask your brothers about that 
stuff when you get home.

00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:22.240
How long did the tenant live in that room?

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:23.590
About three years.

00:13:23.590 --> 00:13:24.480
What did he do?

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:27.990
He said he was a salaryman 
before he moved in.

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:31.360
But he was laid off, 
and his wife and kid left him.

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:33.560
He'd been hopping from job to job since.

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:39.040
I have no idea what he was doing 
inside that apartment by himself.

00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:40.960
Why?

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:43.380
You think you'll find his body?

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:46.970
I'm not saying that, although 
it's true that it smells really bad.

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:49.740
We shouldn't be talking 
about this while we eat.

00:13:50.150 --> 00:13:51.800
How's your first eel?

00:13:51.800 --> 00:13:52.480
Good.

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:56.230
Don't you know any other words?

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:09.070
Hey, is that your house?

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:10.980
Yeah. Why?

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:14.410
Dude, you stink! What happened to you?

00:14:15.150 --> 00:14:16.090
What do you want?

00:14:16.090 --> 00:14:18.040
Damn, my eyes are burning!

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:20.930
Oh, it's nothing. Sorry.

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:38.370
Welcome home. You came 
back filthy again today.

00:14:38.660 --> 00:14:40.640
The bath's ready, so go take one.

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:42.160
You can have dinner after.

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:44.940
What? Are you still mad at me?

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:48.950
Don't touch me.

00:14:50.650 --> 00:14:53.970
Fine. I'm not supposed to 
lay a finger on you, right?

00:14:54.310 --> 00:14:57.270
I stink right now, don't I?

00:14:57.270 --> 00:15:01.040
Yeah, but all you need is a bath.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:03.090
Or did someone say something to you?

00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:06.260
No. It doesn't matter.

00:15:06.530 --> 00:15:07.770
I'm going to take a bath.

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:12.300
<i>I'm the only one who cares about all that.</i>

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:14.790
<i>Like his casual remarks,</i>

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:17.610
<i>or touching and being touched.</i>

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:20.680
<i>The smells, and the sensations.</i>

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:36.540
Huh? Ren fell asleep out here. 
He'll catch a cold.

00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:38.620
You don't need to wake him.

00:15:39.170 --> 00:15:40.580
I'll take him to bed.

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:44.630
Didn't Ren yell at you not 
to lay a finger on him?

00:15:44.870 --> 00:15:46.480
Overconfidence is his greatest enemy.

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:50.010
He's sleeping out here in the open 
after saying those insolent things.

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:52.200
Although that's what makes him cute.

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:55.640
<i>Sometimes I wonder.</i>

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:58.570
<i>Plastic bags and lunch boxes...</i>

00:15:59.260 --> 00:16:03.290
<i>Unopened mail and untouched flyers...</i>

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:08.500
<i>What would it have been like if I'd 
tried to live in Japan by myself?</i>

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:11.910
<i>I still don't really understand 
how to separate garbage.</i>

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:16.830
<i>Haru takes care of all that while working.</i>

00:16:17.630 --> 00:16:22.190
<i>Thanks to him, the apartment was 
always clean while we lived there.</i>

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:25.670
<i>What would happen if I 
suddenly had to live on my own?</i>

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:29.470
<i>What's the difference between the man 
who lived in that room and Haru?</i>

00:16:29.850 --> 00:16:33.710
<i>Haru started living alone 
when he was around my age.</i>

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:36.590
<i>If I were suddenly thrown 
into that situation...</i>

00:16:39.710 --> 00:16:43.260
Are you still asleep? Sheesh.

00:16:46.530 --> 00:16:49.940
What's wrong? I'm right here.

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:52.820
Ow.

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:55.320
Bro, you should learn your lesson already.

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:58.050
What did you do to him this time?

00:16:58.050 --> 00:16:59.700
I didn't do anything.

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:03.830
He was holding onto me in his 
sleep, but when he woke up...

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:05.960
I told you not to touch me!

00:17:07.630 --> 00:17:10.070
Boys his age are so 
complicated and mysterious.

00:17:10.070 --> 00:17:11.210
Isn't that normal?

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:13.920
It just means he's got 
more brains than you.

00:17:16.230 --> 00:17:19.390
We're finally starting 
to see the kitchen floor.

00:17:19.840 --> 00:17:22.840
I don't know how much longer 
we can keep going in this heat.

00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:24.870
You can rest in the house.

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:26.390
I'll work by myself this afternoon.

00:17:26.390 --> 00:17:27.890
What are you talking about?

00:17:27.890 --> 00:17:30.030
You can't even separate garbage.

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:31.240
I'm doing it.

00:17:31.240 --> 00:17:32.300
Liar!

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:35.400
You've just been stuffing 
everything into the same bag.

00:17:35.970 --> 00:17:37.400
It's too much of a hassle.

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:39.440
Well, there is a lot of it.

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:42.230
But we can finally see the rooms in the back.

00:17:42.230 --> 00:17:44.410
Ren, think you can make it to that window?

00:17:46.350 --> 00:17:49.040
Well... I'll try.

00:17:59.900 --> 00:18:01.650
Well done, Ren.

00:18:01.650 --> 00:18:04.240
It wouldn't budge from the outside.

00:18:04.240 --> 00:18:07.350
I'm not surprised. 
There's all kinds of stuff stuck to...

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:10.770
The smell should improve 
with some ventilation.

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:11.590
Gramps...

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:13.110
What do you want for lunch?

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:13.730
Gramps!

00:18:14.050 --> 00:18:17.700
What's with all the noise? 
I'm asking about lunch.

00:18:24.320 --> 00:18:25.200
What is that?

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:29.910
It's a dead dog.

00:18:29.910 --> 00:18:31.710
I-Is he in there, too?

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:35.820
If there were a person rotting in here, 
it would smell worse than this.

00:18:36.310 --> 00:18:39.590
There was dog food in the kitchen, 
so I did think it was strange.

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:43.840
You should've said so sooner.

00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:46.320
I didn't realize he had a dog.

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:49.180
I never heard it bark while
I lived on the second floor.

00:18:49.180 --> 00:18:51.360
Your Tanuki doesn't bark, either.

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:54.190
That's enough for today.

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:57.550
I can't throw out a dog's corpse with 
the rest of the flammable garbage.

00:18:57.550 --> 00:18:59.260
I need to ask the city office.

00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:08.320
<i>One man and one dog.</i>

00:19:13.140 --> 00:19:15.630
Ren, I'm getting sushi for lunch.

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:18.350
Okay. Get it without wasabi.

00:19:18.350 --> 00:19:20.390
And can I borrow your bathroom?

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:23.140
Go ahead. Should I fill the tub for you?

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:25.650
No, I'll just take a shower.

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:28.850
<i>The number you have dialed</i>

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:32.800
<i>can't be reached because it's
either outside the service area</i>

00:19:32.800 --> 00:19:33.980
<i>or currently turned off.</i>

00:19:34.510 --> 00:19:37.630
Haru-san, what are you doing?

00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:39.650
We had an order come in.

00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:43.410
I haven't been able to reach Ren's phone.

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:45.140
Did he turn it off?

00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:47.650
You made him mad again, didn't you?

00:19:47.650 --> 00:19:49.320
Shima-kun told me all about it.

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:52.920
Yeah, but there's no point in 
having a phone if you turn it off.

00:19:53.220 --> 00:19:57.390
Won't the fact that you 
don't get that he's silently

00:19:57.390 --> 00:19:59.680
protesting make him even madder?

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:04.430
And you're something of an idiot 
for annoying me about that.

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:08.090
By the way, did Kiyoka-san tell you?

00:20:08.090 --> 00:20:10.430
There's a second Natsu in Kabukicho!

00:20:10.430 --> 00:20:11.840
A second Natsu?

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:14.090
He's a super popular host right now.

00:20:14.090 --> 00:20:15.080
I'm not interested.

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:17.730
Since he goes by the same name you used,

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:21.450
a lot of customers go there hoping 
you've returned to the business.

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:23.720
And it's not just his name.

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:27.400
His build's a lot like yours, 
so everyone's talking about it.

00:20:27.400 --> 00:20:30.700
There are plenty of guys who look like me.

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:32.590
Are you trying to pick a fight?

00:20:32.590 --> 00:20:35.970
When we were hosts, you left 
us to make tons of money!

00:20:35.970 --> 00:20:40.410
If the world's full of guys 
like you, I'll hang myself!

00:20:40.410 --> 00:20:44.480
It's okay. The world's pretty 
full of guys like you, too.

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:47.220
You mean I'm "one of many others," don't you?!

00:20:47.410 --> 00:20:51.360
No, I mean nice guys who lack confidence

00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:54.230
and care too much about 
what other people think.

00:20:54.580 --> 00:20:56.160
Well, sorry about that!

00:20:56.160 --> 00:20:58.860
Don't worry about it. 
I was talking about myself.

00:21:00.140 --> 00:21:03.780
But you seem as far removed 
from all that as possible.

00:21:07.240 --> 00:21:07.920
Huh?

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:14.920
Are you that middle schooler 
from the other day?

00:21:15.180 --> 00:21:16.560
I'm not a middle schooler.

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:18.810
You have the wrong person.

00:21:19.970 --> 00:21:22.540
Hey, you don't stink today.

00:21:22.540 --> 00:21:24.430
You smell like soap.

00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:25.760
Who are you?

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:28.030
Who, me? Natsu.

00:21:28.480 --> 00:21:30.520
Your brother's name is Natsu, too, right?

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:33.770
I've been running into a lot 
of trouble because of that.

00:21:34.270 --> 00:21:38.230
I thought I'd see what he looked like 
for myself, but I changed my mind.

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:41.410
We should go on a date. Good idea, right?

00:21:42.030 --> 00:21:43.030
L-Let go!

00:21:43.510 --> 00:21:44.640
Let go!

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:48.350
Ren?

00:21:54.590 --> 00:21:57.170
<i>Who is this guy?</i>

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:40.280
Next Time
